<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37786" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-nāvĭgo</span></b> ,
			āvi, 1, v. a. and n.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to sail by</i>
			or <i>past</i> any thing, <i>to sail
				along</i> (post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>absol.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praenavigantes adulterae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 51, 12</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 23, 26, §
			97</span></i>.—With <i>acc.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praenavigans litus, loca,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mel.
					2, 3, 6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Val.
				Max. 1, 8, 9</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oppida praenavigari tradunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					6, 28, 32, § 146</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 3, 6</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to sail past</i>,
				<i>to hurry past</i> a thing: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praenavigamus vitam,</span>”
				<i>pass</i>, <i>spend</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 70, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
